// Test check: the whole raycast state -- x, z, steps taken and the done flag,
// each under its name -- so a case about the loop that walks it states where
// the ray ended up and whether it stopped. ray_loop reads the step count and
// the flag itself, so a check of either one alone would repeat its own read.
rc_state() {
  string rcs_s = "x=" + (import rc)[0] + " z=" + (import rc)[1];
  rcs_s = rcs_s + " steps=" + (import rc)[2] + " done=" + (import rc)[3];
} return string rcs_s;
given ray_init(1000, 2000) ():("x=1000 z=2000 steps=0 done=0")
given ray_init(555, 999) ():("x=555 z=999 steps=0 done=0")
